WEBVTT

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:11.199
Hi there.

00:00:11.199 --> 00:00:13.791
Welcome to this video
where we are going to learn

00:00:13.791 --> 00:00:16.799
how to protect your personal data online.

00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:20.319
Personal data
does not disappear on its own.

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:23.359
You can take steps to stay safe
and stay in control.

00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:27.983
The goal of this video is to show
simple ways to protect your privacy.

00:00:29.039 --> 00:00:31.951
We will look 
at privacy settings, app permissions,

00:00:31.951 --> 00:00:35.391
safe sharing habits, 
and deleting old information.

00:00:35.871 --> 00:00:38.879
These small actions
can make a big difference.

00:00:43.279 --> 00:00:46.767
Protecting personal data
means controlling who can see it

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:50.847
and how it is used
when you use apps and websites.

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:53.887
They may collect and store 
information about you.

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:57.839
Privacy tools help you choose
what is shared and what is not.

00:00:58.527 --> 00:01:03.119
Many apps have privacy settings
like Public friends or only me.

00:01:03.999 --> 00:01:06.399
Public means many people can see it.

00:01:07.375 --> 00:01:11.823
Choosing "only friends" can reduce 
who sees your posts and information.

00:01:12.463 --> 00:01:15.023
Before posting a photo, 
check the background.

00:01:15.023 --> 00:01:18.303
Could it show your school name,
a street sign, or your house number?

00:01:18.975 --> 00:01:21.423
Even if your face is not shown,

00:01:21.423 --> 00:01:24.415
background  details can still 
reveal private information.

00:01:25.535 --> 00:01:29.375
Using a nickname instead of a full name
can help protect privacy.

00:01:30.015 --> 00:01:34.175
Try not to share your address, phone
number, or school name in public spaces.

00:01:34.783 --> 00:01:38.015
If a website asks for information
that feels unnecessary,

00:01:38.095 --> 00:01:41.103
stop and ask a trusted adult.

00:01:41.695 --> 00:01:44.400
Apps sometimes ask for permissions

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.775
like access to your camera,
microphone, photos, or location.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.247
Permissions should match what the app needs.

00:01:51.247 --> 00:01:55.407
If a simple game asks for location,
that could be a warning sign.

00:01:57.039 --> 00:02:01.199
Logging out helps protect your accounts,
especially on shared devices.

00:02:04.495 --> 00:02:06.543
Locking your device with a passcode

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:09.743
keeps other people 
from opening your apps and messages.

00:02:10.383 --> 00:02:13.967
These are simple steps
that protect your personal data every day.

00:02:15.743 --> 00:02:21.103
Old accounts and old posts can keep 
your data online longer than you expect.

00:02:21.263 --> 00:02:25.663
If you no longer use an app, deleting
the account can reduce stored data.

00:02:26.351 --> 00:02:32.543
If you posted something by mistake,
deleting it quickly can limit who sees it.

00:02:32.751 --> 00:02:37.151
If something feels strange
or unsafe, report it and ask for help.


00:02:37.503 --> 00:02:40.702
You can tell a trusted adult, 
a teacher or a parent.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:45.342
Getting help quickly is a smart way
to protect your data and your safety.

00:02:46.782 --> 00:02:49.982
One helpful habit 
is to use a clean up checklist.

00:02:50.622 --> 00:02:54.094
For example, check privacy
settings, review permissions.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:57.102
Delete old apps and log out.

00:02:57.102 --> 00:03:01.214
Doing a small cleanup regularly 
keeps your digital footprint smaller.

00:03:05.198 --> 00:03:06.670
Let's recap.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.742
Protecting personal data
means sharing carefully,

00:03:09.758 --> 00:03:12.910
using privacy settings 
and checking permissions.

00:03:13.598 --> 00:03:14.350
Log out.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:18.190
Delete what you do not need
and ask a trusted adult when unsure.

00:03:19.646 --> 00:03:22.638
You have the power to control your data
and protect your privacy

00:03:24.046 --> 00:03:25.038
Great work!

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:27.966
In this video,
you learned practical ways to protect

00:03:27.966 --> 00:03:30.958
your personal data online.

00:03:31.022 --> 00:03:32.590
Thank you for watching.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.406
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.